            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The legal minimum tread depth in NSW is 1.5mm, which is level with the tread wear indicators in the grooves. Replace tyres sooner if you see cracks, bulges or uneven wear, and have tyres older than 5 years checked even if the tread looks fine."
